WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.701
-On the eve of the
midterm elections,

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.033
the Republican Party has made
their agenda crystal clear.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:06.834
If they regain power,
they will once again

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.901
thrust our government into chaos

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.834
while subverting
future elections

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.634
to cement permanent
Republican rule.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.934
And they've also made clear
that Donald Trump is still

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.834
and will remain
the leader of their party

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.534
and that they will march
in lockstep behind him

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:19.734
if they win on Tuesday.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.801
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:24.100
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.934
If you watch Republican
midterm ads

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.367
or listen to Republicans talk,

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.334
they pretend that they're
focused on issues like crime

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:32.868
or gas prices or inflation.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:36.100
Dr. Mehmet Oz, the GOP candidate
for Senate in Pennsylvania,

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.667
tried to highlight gas prices

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.934
by posting this incredibly
bizarre picture of himself

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:42.667
standing under a sign
showing gas prices

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.567
at a Sheetz convenience store

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:45.834
on the side of the road
in Altoona,

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:48.033
just hanging out
under a gas station sign,

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.467
you know, like
ordinary Americans do.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.601
So stoic, too.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:57.467
He looks like a car dealership
tube man after he quit caffeine.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:58.834
There are actually
a few more things

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:00.734
I want to zoom in on,
in this picture,

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.767
as part of our new segment,
"An Even Closer Look."

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:05.033
[ Theme music plays ]

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:06.801
Alright, first of all,
why are his arms crossed

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:10.567
like he's doing a pose in the
opening credits of "Shark Tank"?

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:12.901
"So, you want to sell pills
that don't do anything?

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.033
I'm intrigued."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.834
Also, I love his serious face.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:21.133
Look at him.
He's a gas station bouncer.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:24.734
"Sir, you're not on the list.
Get your beef jerky elsewhere.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:26.801
Ladies, right this way."

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:29.400
And I'm sorry, there's only one
Pennsylvania Senate candidate

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.167
who can pull off
the nightclub bouncer look.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.868
I mean, that's a guy
who will not be fooled

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.400
by your out-of-state I.D.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.601
Plus, Fetterman is so tall that
when he takes the same picture,

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.934
gas looks like
it's only $0.99.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:45.400
And finally,
let's zoom in Oz' feet.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:48.868
Why is he standing
on a tiny rock?

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:50.400
Does he think
he's stranded at sea?

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.133
Is he playing
"the floor is lava"?

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:55.667
Or more likely, is he wearing
super expensive shoes?

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:58.567
"I stand for all Pennsylvanians
on a tiny rock

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:01.634
so I don't get dirt
on my Brunello Cucinellis."

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.434
This has been
"An Even Closer Look."

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.200
[ Theme music plays ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.567
So, Republicans claim
they're focused on issues.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:11.968
"Oh, but Seth," you might say,
"didn't you just spend 2 minutes

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.701
making fun
of a picture of Dr. Oz?"

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.100
Yes, but I never claim
to be focused on the issues.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.534
Republicans did.

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.400
And when you press them
for specifics

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.334
on what they would actually do
if they win,

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.667
they don't really have any.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.400
That's what happened
when Florida Senator Rick Scott,

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.234
who's in charge of taking
back the Senate

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:29.934
for Republicans this year,
went on "Meet the Press"

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:32.834
and was asked if he could name
a bill Republicans would pass

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:35.200
that President Biden
might actually sign into law.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.868
And instead, he just repeated

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.934
a bunch of
lazy Republican slogans.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.834
-Alright, let's assume
you've got the majority.

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:42.234
I'm gonna take you
at your word.

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:43.834
You're gonna get the House.
You're gonna get the Senate.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:46.901
What's the first bill
a Republican Congress

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.467
sends to
the president's desk

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:51.234
that you actually think
he would sign?

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:53.501
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:54.934
-I think the issues --

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:56.501
we've got to deal
with inflation.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:58.801
So we've got to figure out
how to spend our money wisely

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:00.767
so we don't continue
this inflation.

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:02.300
I think we've got to do
whatever we can

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.467
to get this crime rate down.

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:04.667
So I think we have
to look at that.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.100
We've got to secure the border.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.267
So I think those are the things
that we have to focus on.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:10.000
-Yeah, but
none of those are bills.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.434
We can all name issues.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:12.901
You know, we're asking
for solutions.

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:14.467
When you go to the doctor,
he doesn't just point out

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.767
a bunch of [Bleep] that's wrong
with you and leave.

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:18.634
"Well, we've got to do something
about the gallbladder,

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:19.801
and that heart's no good.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:21.567
Plus, a bunch of your bones
are out of place,

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:22.734
and you need a new kidney.

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:24.267
Anyway, good luck
with all of that.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:27.901
I'm gonna go hang out under
the sign at the gas station

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:30.634
with the other 'doctors.'"

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.300
So, once again,
Republicans are making promises

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.834
they obviously have
no intention of keeping.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.501
How many times do we have to go
through this dance with the GOP

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:37.901
before we learn
that they're lying?

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.334
Remember when they did
the same thing with Obamacare?

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:41.934
For almost an entire decade,

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.801
they said
Obamacare had to be repealed,

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:45.367
that it was
their number-one priority,

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:48.834
and that they had a solution
that would be so much better

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:51.901
and cost so much less and
give everyone great healthcare?

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:53.534
Remember when
Trump said all this?

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.667
-We are coming up with something

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.434
that I believe
will be very good.

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:02.033
A bill that's going to be
a phenomenal bill.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.934
We're going to have something
that's going to be

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:07.367
much more understood
and much more popular

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.334
than people can even imagine.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:12.300
This will be a plan where
you can choose your doctor.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.167
This will be a plan
where you can choose your plan.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:17.667
And you know what the plan is?
This is the plan.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.267
This is a great bill.
There's a great plan.

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.701
And this will be
great healthcare.

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:25.968
You're going to have
such great healthcare

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:28.767
at a tiny fraction of the cost,

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.601
and it's gonna be so easy.

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:33.067
-As usual, with Trump,
he couldn't stop overpromising.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:35.767
It's one thing to lie and say
you have a plan when you don't.

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:39.100
It's another to say that
nonexistent plan you don't have

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.000
is the greatest plan
to ever exist

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.434
in the history of civilization.

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.834
"This plan is so amazing.
You're gonna get everything --

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.601
perfect healthcare,
completely free.

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:49.033
And if you like your doctor,
you can keep your doctor.

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:50.968
You can keep him
in your basement,

00:04:50.968 --> 00:04:52.701
chained to a wall."

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:55.434
And they'll be there 24/7
to serve your medical needs.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.567
The doctors don't like it,
but you're gonna love it.

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.267
You're gonna love it."

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:02.334
Also, remember when he said
it would be so easy?

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:05.834
Like he was a dude trying
to impress a date at a carnival.

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:07.300
"Hey, babe,
you want that giant bear?

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.567
No problem.
Gonna be so easy.

00:05:08.567 --> 00:05:10.300
I can hit that clown's mouth
in one shot.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.567
[Bleep]
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:15.534
Not even close! Damn it!

00:05:15.534 --> 00:05:18.000
The clown moved!
I swear, the clown moved, babe!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.934
No! No!

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:22.000
I won't let it go!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.300
You don't understand!

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.133
I'm gonna go to the Sheetz
and hang out under the sign!"

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:29.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.367
Now, that's two.

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:34.334
That's two callbacks
to the Sheetz sign.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.167
So, if you know
anything about comedy,

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:39.033
there's probably --
probably one more coming.

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:41.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:44.167
You're not out of the woods yet,
"Dr. Oz."

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:46.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.734
Anyway, Trump
was, of course, lying,

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:49.467
just like the rest
of the Republican Party,

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:51.400
when it came time
to actually pass a bill

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.968
to replace Obamacare
after nearly a decade.

00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:56.767
I'm realizing now it was a gun,
and I threw a ball.

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:58.400
Right?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.400
Mm-hmm. It just dawned on me.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.701
I'm mime-throwing,

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:03.400
and it's gonna be
a tricky edit.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:11.167
When it came time to actually
pass a bill to replace Obamacare

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:13.400
after nearly a decade
of empty promises,

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.968
they freaked out like a
hung-over college freshman

00:06:15.968 --> 00:06:17.901
waking up in his dorm room
at 6:00 a.m.

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.868
with a blank piece of paper
stuck to his face.

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:22.934
"Oh, [Bleep]!
Oh, this is due in an hour!

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:24.734
Oh, let's see.
What do I have so far?

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:27.534
'This will be a thesis where
you can choose your thesis.

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:30.300
and you know what the thesis is,
this is the thesis.'

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.300
Ohh, aw!"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:37.467
The same thing is playing out
all over again.

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:40.133
Except this time,
all the lies and empty promises

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.567
are concealing something
much more nefarious.

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:45.200
And that is the real reason
Republicans want power,

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.067
so they can rig future elections

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:48.734
and install permanent
one-party rule.

00:06:48.734 --> 00:06:50.400
And that's not
just me saying that.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:54.000
Republicans are saying that.
They are saying it in public,

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.367
out in the open,
for everyone to hear.

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:56.968
The GOP candidate
for governor in Wisconsin,

00:06:56.968 --> 00:06:59.100
Tim Michels,
who is in a dead heat

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.033
with the Democratic incumbent,
Tony Evers,

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:02.767
said at a campaign stop
last week,

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:06.067
"Republicans will never lose
another election in Wisconsin

00:07:06.067 --> 00:07:07.167
after I'm elected governor."

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:09.334
That wasn't even
a secret confession

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:11.467
caught on hidden camera
at a private event.

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:13.200
He said that at
a public campaign stop.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.934
It used to be that
when you caught politicians

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:16.234
confessing
to something scandalous,

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:18.234
it would be on grainy
black-and-white footage

00:07:18.234 --> 00:07:19.667
from a motel security camera.

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:21.467
Now they just yell it
into a microphone

00:07:21.467 --> 00:07:23.334
like Michael Buffer
before a boxing match.

00:07:23.334 --> 00:07:27.167
"Let's get ready for fascism!"

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:31.200
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.634
By the way, not the real song.

00:07:32.634 --> 00:07:35.267
It's a fake sound, like
we couldn't afford the real one,

00:07:35.267 --> 00:07:38.000
thanks to inflation.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.033
[ Laughter ]
Anyway, the point is,

00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:42.834
the thing that really
motivates Republicans

00:07:42.834 --> 00:07:44.834
is not the cost of living
or gas prices

00:07:44.834 --> 00:07:46.767
or any of that stuff.
It's election denialism.

00:07:46.767 --> 00:07:48.601
Trump's big lie
about the 2020 election

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.901
is now the beating heart
of conservative ideology.

00:07:50.901 --> 00:07:52.534
It's their single
obsessive focus

00:07:52.534 --> 00:07:53.968
and the thing
that galvanizes them,

00:07:53.968 --> 00:07:57.133
as you can see from a rally
Trump held in Miami last night

00:07:57.133 --> 00:07:58.601
for Florida Senator Marco Rubio,

00:07:58.601 --> 00:08:01.400
where the crowd
actually chanted with Trump

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.234
when he claimed
the 2020 election was stolen.

00:08:03.234 --> 00:08:04.667
And by the way,
just for the record,

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:05.834
what you're about
to hear from Trump,

00:08:05.834 --> 00:08:07.767
as if you even needed
to hear me say this,

00:08:07.767 --> 00:08:09.400
is complete and utter nonsense.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:13.434
Just this week, the Pennsylvania
Supreme Court ruled, in effect,

00:08:13.434 --> 00:08:16.167
that I was 100% right,

00:08:16.167 --> 00:08:19.400
and the 2020 presidential
election in Pennsylvania

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.834
was riddled with ballots

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:24.300
that should never
have been counted.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:26.801
Far more
than necessary to win.

00:08:26.801 --> 00:08:30.501
They stated that big things
that took place

00:08:30.501 --> 00:08:32.601
in 2020
presidential election

00:08:32.601 --> 00:08:35.100
in Pennsylvania
were not allowed.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.834
They weren't allowed to do it.

00:08:36.834 --> 00:08:39.968
Now, they did it anyway.
But they weren't allowed.

00:08:39.968 --> 00:08:43.567
But they refused the court
to invalidate the election.

00:08:43.567 --> 00:08:46.467
Instead, in the future,
they say.

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:48.367
[ Chuckles ]

00:08:48.367 --> 00:08:50.234
That's true. That's true.

00:08:56.167 --> 00:08:57.467
By a lot.

00:08:57.467 --> 00:08:59.634
-You know...
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.634 --> 00:09:02.167
You know how when
you read Supreme Court opinions,

00:09:02.167 --> 00:09:03.534
they always use language

00:09:03.534 --> 00:09:05.901
like, "Big things took place
that were not allowed."

00:09:05.901 --> 00:09:07.767
[ Laughter ]
You can read all about it

00:09:07.767 --> 00:09:10.501
in Trump v.
Bad Guys, Nasty Guys.

00:09:10.501 --> 00:09:13.701
But that's what really gets
Republicans going, not --

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:14.934
You can notice,
they're not chanting,

00:09:14.934 --> 00:09:16.601
"Solve inflation
or balance the budget."

00:09:16.601 --> 00:09:19.467
Also in general, whenever an
angry mob is chanting something,

00:09:19.467 --> 00:09:22.367
you want a politician
who will try to calm them down,

00:09:22.367 --> 00:09:24.300
not respond by saying,
"That's true."

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:26.267
When the townsfolk
showed up with torches

00:09:26.267 --> 00:09:28.267
and pitchforks
to kill Frankenstein,

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:29.567
Trump probably
would have been there saying,

00:09:29.567 --> 00:09:30.734
"You know what?
You guys are right.

00:09:30.734 --> 00:09:32.901
We have to kill
that giant green monster.

00:09:32.901 --> 00:09:34.634
We got to kill him
with the bolts in his neck.

00:09:34.634 --> 00:09:36.667
Personally, I've always been
more of a Dracula fan.

00:09:36.667 --> 00:09:39.133
We love Dracula, don't we?
We love Dracula.

00:09:39.133 --> 00:09:42.367
I met him during a presidential
visit to Transylvania.

00:09:42.367 --> 00:09:44.767
I was there.
He came up to me.

00:09:44.767 --> 00:09:47.300
a big guy, tough guy,
tears pouring up his face,

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:50.701
because he was hanging
by his feet like a bat.

00:09:50.701 --> 00:09:52.934
So the tears were dripping
from his eyes,

00:09:52.934 --> 00:09:54.267
down his forehead,
onto the floor.

00:09:54.267 --> 00:09:56.133
It was very special.
He said to me, 'Mr. Trump, sir,

00:09:56.133 --> 00:09:57.467
I want to suck your blood.'

00:09:57.467 --> 00:10:00.534
And I said, 'Dracula,
you remind me of my son.'"

00:10:00.534 --> 00:10:02.501
Although...
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:05.234
...my favorite crowd chant
during that rally

00:10:05.234 --> 00:10:07.467
came when Trump was ranting
about his first impeachment --

00:10:07.467 --> 00:10:09.634
the one where he tried
to extort Ukraine

00:10:09.634 --> 00:10:11.400
to help him cheat
in the 2020 election.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.567
And he attacked one of
the lead impeachment managers,

00:10:13.567 --> 00:10:14.901
Congressman Adam Schiff.

00:10:14.901 --> 00:10:16.734
-So, the speech he made

00:10:16.734 --> 00:10:18.968
was total you-know-what.

00:10:18.968 --> 00:10:21.434
I won't use it, because
my wife always says --

00:10:21.434 --> 00:10:23.434
she always says, "Darling,

00:10:23.434 --> 00:10:25.734
don't use the word
'bull[Bleep].'"

00:10:25.734 --> 00:10:28.000
So I'm not gonna use it.
I'm telling you -- first lady.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.534
"'[Bleep]' --
Don't use that word."

00:10:39.033 --> 00:10:41.868
Wow, you guys are the coolest
kids in fifth grade.

00:10:41.868 --> 00:10:43.367
[ Laughter ]

00:10:43.367 --> 00:10:45.000
"We got a substitute teacher
today.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.267
Let's all chant '[Bleep]'
and see if he cries."

00:10:47.267 --> 00:10:49.167
[ Laughter ]

00:10:49.167 --> 00:10:50.934
But Trump remains obsessed
with the election

00:10:50.934 --> 00:10:52.801
and with his two impeachments,
which is why

00:10:52.801 --> 00:10:55.100
Republicans have made it clear
that one of the first things

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:56.501
they'll do if they
get back in power

00:10:56.501 --> 00:10:58.701
is use Congress to investigate
their political enemies,

00:10:58.701 --> 00:11:00.567
impeach various
Cabinet officials,

00:11:00.567 --> 00:11:02.767
like Merrick Garland,
prosecute Dr. Anthony Fauci,

00:11:02.767 --> 00:11:04.267
and even impeach Biden himself,

00:11:04.267 --> 00:11:06.367
which has led
former President Barack Obama

00:11:06.367 --> 00:11:07.667
to add a little comedy routine

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:10.400
to his stump speech
about how ridiculous that is.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.601
-They're on record.

00:11:11.601 --> 00:11:12.901
If they get control of Congress,

00:11:12.901 --> 00:11:15.367
they will spend
the next two years

00:11:15.367 --> 00:11:19.767
investigating President Biden
and their political opponents.

00:11:19.767 --> 00:11:22.801
That's all they want to do.
They see it as payback.

00:11:22.801 --> 00:11:24.501
Some of them have said

00:11:24.501 --> 00:11:27.334
they're going to impeach
President Biden.

00:11:27.334 --> 00:11:30.400
Now, they're not sure why.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:33.567
They're not sure what for yet.

00:11:33.567 --> 00:11:36.234
But, apparently,
that's beside the point.

00:11:36.234 --> 00:11:38.367
-You know, we've said it before
and we'll say it again.

00:11:38.367 --> 00:11:40.501
One of the only good things
about campaign season

00:11:40.501 --> 00:11:43.100
is the return
of stand-up comedy Obama.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:45.968
"Let's see.
What else? What else?

00:11:45.968 --> 00:11:50.067
You see that photo of Dr. Oz?
What's up with this weird dude?

00:11:50.067 --> 00:11:55.434
Standing on the side of the road
like a restaurant mascot.

00:11:55.434 --> 00:11:56.934
I said to Michelle -- I said,
'I didn't know

00:11:56.934 --> 00:11:59.100
they had a Bob's Little Boy.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.901
[ Laughter ]

00:12:01.901 --> 00:12:05.601
This ain't New Jersey.
You got to pump your own gas.

00:12:05.601 --> 00:12:07.501
Dried-up,
Spock-looking mother[Bleep]."

00:12:07.501 --> 00:12:09.400
[ Laughter ]

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:10.834
And there's it.
That's the third.

00:12:10.834 --> 00:12:13.000
That's it.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.334
Anyway, that's what Republicans
are gonna do.

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:17.634
They're gonna use the levers
of political -- of power

00:12:17.634 --> 00:12:20.167
for political retribution
and to plunge our government

00:12:20.167 --> 00:12:22.400
and our economy into crisis
after crisis after crisis.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.767
Again, this isn't a weird
conspiracy theory I made up.

00:12:24.767 --> 00:12:27.033
This is all just stuff they've
said themselves in public.

00:12:27.033 --> 00:12:30.067
They want to impeach Biden
and his cabinet,

00:12:30.067 --> 00:12:32.367
investigated Fauci,
pass a national abortion ban,

00:12:32.367 --> 00:12:33.667
hold the debt ceiling hostage

00:12:33.667 --> 00:12:35.901
to force cuts to
Social Security and Medicare,

00:12:35.901 --> 00:12:37.033
which among other things,

00:12:37.033 --> 00:12:38.734
could potentially
detonate our economy.

00:12:38.734 --> 00:12:40.767
That's all stuff
they've said on the record.

00:12:40.767 --> 00:12:43.234
It will be the Trump era
over and over again.

00:12:43.234 --> 00:12:45.300
Nonstop crisis,
Nonstop chaos, nonstop...

00:12:47.501 --> 00:12:50.267
But most important of all,
they want to use their positions

00:12:50.267 --> 00:12:53.234
in key states across the country
to rig future elections

00:12:53.234 --> 00:12:54.701
and cement one-party
Republican rule.

00:12:54.701 --> 00:12:57.133
The GOP candidate for
secretary of state in Nevada,

00:12:57.133 --> 00:12:58.634
Jim Marchant, who openly said

00:12:58.634 --> 00:13:00.868
he and other pro-Trump
secretaries of state

00:13:00.868 --> 00:13:02.467
around the country
will make sure

00:13:02.467 --> 00:13:04.901
that Trump wins,
no matter what, in 2024.

00:13:04.901 --> 00:13:06.534
-We have something in common.

00:13:06.534 --> 00:13:09.534
President Trump and I
lost an election in 2020

00:13:09.534 --> 00:13:12.701
because of a rigged election.
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:13:12.701 --> 00:13:15.167
And when I'm secretary of state
of Nevada,

00:13:15.167 --> 00:13:16.567
we're gonna fix it.

00:13:16.567 --> 00:13:19.367
And when my coalition
of secretary of state candidates

00:13:19.367 --> 00:13:21.267
around the country
get elected,

00:13:21.267 --> 00:13:23.234
we're gonna fix
the whole country,

00:13:23.234 --> 00:13:27.901
and President Trump is gonna be
president again in 2024.

00:13:27.901 --> 00:13:29.801
-Once again, they're just
admitting their plans

00:13:29.801 --> 00:13:32.000
to steal
the 2024 election in advance.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.167
Seriously, what else
do we have to do

00:13:33.167 --> 00:13:34.634
to get people
to pay attention to this?

00:13:34.634 --> 00:13:37.033
Do I have to stand on
a street corner in Times Square,

00:13:37.033 --> 00:13:38.234
dressed like Abe Lincoln,

00:13:38.234 --> 00:13:39.934
handing out pamphlets
like one of those guys

00:13:39.934 --> 00:13:41.334
advertising
a Presidents' Day sale?

00:13:41.334 --> 00:13:42.701
Because I will do it.

00:13:42.701 --> 00:13:45.868
Actually, I won't do it,
but I will make Wally do it.

00:13:45.868 --> 00:13:47.601
-[ Clears throat ]

00:13:47.601 --> 00:13:51.267
Four score and seven
cue cards -- Oh.

00:13:51.267 --> 00:13:54.667
[ Laughter ]

00:13:54.667 --> 00:13:56.868
-God.

00:13:56.868 --> 00:13:58.667
It's like...

00:13:58.667 --> 00:14:00.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:03.334 --> 00:14:06.400
It's like a dead heat
with Daniel Day-Lewis.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.267
[ Laughter ]

00:14:08.267 --> 00:14:11.100
It's very possible the Democrats
will lose seats tomorrow,

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.801
since historically
that always is what happens

00:14:13.801 --> 00:14:16.133
to the party in power.
In fact, it would be very normal

00:14:16.133 --> 00:14:18.067
and maybe even unremarkable
if it weren't for the fact

00:14:18.067 --> 00:14:20.167
that Republicans want
to subvert the system

00:14:20.167 --> 00:14:22.534
to ensure that they
never lose power again.

00:14:22.534 --> 00:14:24.767
That's their plan.
And we know that's their plan

00:14:24.767 --> 00:14:26.734
because they've said
that's their plan.

00:14:26.734 --> 00:14:28.667
It's a plan...
-Where you can choose your plan.

00:14:28.667 --> 00:14:31.367
And you know what the plan is?
This is the plan.

00:14:31.367 --> 00:14:33.434
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:33.434 --> 00:14:36.968
[ Theme music plays ]

00:14:36.968 --> 00:14:38.834
The midterm elections
are coming up.

00:14:38.834 --> 00:14:41.400
So to make sure that you're
good to vote in this election,

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.601
visit our good friends
at headcount.org

00:14:44.601 --> 00:14:46.534
to check your
voter-registration status

00:14:46.534 --> 00:14:48.300
or to register to vote.

